# 16. Refresh plan — every 3 days

Per the Skills Playbook, this pillar updates on a 3-day cycle. The refresh must change enough to signal freshness to Google without breaking structure or losing schema validation.

| **Cycle element** | **What changes** | **What must stay** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Opening paragraph (Section 3 or 4) | 2–3 sentences reworded with the same core message | Direct AEO answer (first 2 sentences in Section 3) — verbatim |
| FAQs (Section 14) | Rotate 2 FAQs: retire the 2 lowest-performing, add 2 new ones pulled from Search Console + People Also Ask | Minimum count: 24. Banned words: 0 |
| Practice questions (Section 9) | Swap 3 questions (one per difficulty level) | Total count: 70. Answer quality: teacher-voice explanations |
| Exam date / year references | Update if an official date changes | Structure of Section 5 table |
| Last-reviewed timestamp (metadata) | Auto-update on every publish | — |

### Validator checklist (from the Skills Playbook — every refresh must pass)

- Structure — all required H1/H2/H3 present; no accidental heading deletion.

- Banned words — zero occurrences.

- Heading ratio — ≤ 65% of headings match the primary keyword.

- Internal links — minimum count preserved; no broken outbound links.

- Schema.org — Course / FAQPage / BreadcrumbList / ItemList all validate.

- Freshness — last-reviewed date updated; at least one body change present.

