# 18. Humanization checklist — this draft's pass/fail

The 8-point humanization checklist from the Skills Playbook. A page does not ship until every item passes.

| **Check** | **Status** | **Where it lives** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Has an 'Explain like I'm 15' plain-language section | PASS | Section 4 (Is AP HuG hard?) + every unit summary in Section 6 |
| At least one real-world example tied to each concept | PASS | Every sample question in Section 9 + every unit summary |
| 'Common mistakes students make' block | PASS | Per-unit “Most common trap” callout in Section 6 |
| At least one AP-specific exam tip | PASS | Exam-tip line under every one of 70 questions in Section 9 |
| Zero banned words | PASS | Draft written against the banned-words list; validator will reconfirm |
| ≤ 65% of headings match primary keyword | PASS | Section headings vary; keyword density ~ 40% |
| Intro opens with a hook, not a definition | PASS | Section 3 expansion and Section 4 open with a question and pattern, not a definition |
| FAQ answers put the direct answer in the first 2 sentences | PASS | All 24 FAQs in Section 14 |

*End of document  ·  Ready for page-builder import  ·  APScore5 Confidential Draft*

